# Part C — Potentiality and Composition

## 9. Potentiality, not probability

The Locale field's primitive is potentiality: a real, not-yet-actualized capacity that can hold contraries without collapsing them, rather than a real non-negative number. This repair is necessary — a bare probability cannot host interference — but on its own it only relocates the problem to §10.

## 10. The composition problem — partially discharged

**[OPEN → partially discharged]** How do potentialities compose to produce a phase term, a Born rule, an interference pattern? No composition law was ever written down for Lumen itself.

A candidate now exists, imported from Pentakinetics §13: two internally recursive structures coupled **multiplicatively** rather than additively —

$$\text{loop}_A \times \text{loop}_B$$

— with an argument attached: under addition, costly improvements are selected away before they pay off; multiplication produces the nonlinear regime in which an improvement anywhere raises the return on improvements elsewhere.

**[OBLIGATION]** — that argument was built in a selection-economics context (comparative cognition). Transferring it to potentiality composition requires showing the reasoning actually carries over, not importing the conclusion on the strength of the analogy. Undischarged.

